crop160_span_s2026.pt       # 0.8564 — the 160 mm field at 420 px, mm/px held (0.381 vs the 130 mm
# recipe's 0.387). Added 2026-09-02. Rostered as SHIPPABLE, not as a seat claim: it clears the 0.8521
# non-DINOv2 bar and it is the only member fitted at a field wider than 130 mm, so it is the pool's one
# reading of coverage going OUT. It is NOT better than its control — band_span 0.8565, delta -0.0001,
# which is the arm's own NULL branch on the mean.
#
# THE PER-FINDING SPLIT IS WHY IT IS HERE. crop80_span cropped IN and lost MCL -0.0265 and ACL -0.0263
# TOGETHER, and the decode-geometry family was closed on reading those two as one margin effect. Going
# OUT they move in OPPOSITE directions: MCL +0.0086 (0.7955 vs 0.7869), ACL -0.0124 (0.8730 vs 0.8854).
# One mechanism cannot produce a paired loss going in and a split going out, so the margin story is
# wrong about at least one of the two structures.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT LICENSE. Both moves are inside per-label noise — the 0.0062 floor is on the MEAN and
# a single label carries fewer positives, so its half-width is wider, not narrower. This is DIRECTIONAL
# and it does not re-open the decode-geometry family. The ledger's closure stands on the mean; what it
# loses is the explanation, not the verdict.

# 2026-09-02 — three that finished and were never written down. Scored here before adding: all three
# clear the 0.8459 merit bar and the 0.8521 non-DINOv2 bar, on the same 909-study holdout as every
# other seat, so there is no argument for declining them.
ramp_dense_gate.pt                  # 0.8578 peak e7 — the ramp recipe with the dense gate. Seated on MERIT
                                    # and on the same split its two siblings below are seated on: the
                                    # checkpoint clears both bars, the LEVER is closed by the three-arm
                                    # family read. It carried a contradicting decline from before that split
                                    # was drawn, retired 2026-09-03 (the argument is kept, commented, in
                                    # comp/members.declines). This line read 0.8579 until then; two of the
                                    # three places that quote it say 0.8578, which is the peak-epoch number.
stack_increments_base_s2026.pt      # 0.8635, e9 — second-best solo the pool holds
stack_increments_fx_s2026_run1.pt   # 0.8595, e6 — the fx twin's first run; the second is TRUNCATED
certainty_ramp_s2026.pt     # 0.8584 peak e8, CONVERGED (12 of 12, convergence_check clean). Clears the 0.8459
                            # merit level and outscores twenty seated members. Seated on merit, NOT on the ramp
                            # lever: against its own control calib_dense_hold_s2026 (0.8634) it reads -0.0050,
                            # and its two siblings land inside noise of it (disagreed_ramp 0.8574,
                            # ramp_dense_gate 0.8578, which is declined on exactly that control delta). Three
                            # converged ramp arms spanning 0.8574-0.8584 against a 0.8634 control is a
                            # three-arm family read pointing DOWN: the certainty ramp does not pay at this
                            # operating point. What seats here is the CHECKPOINT; the LEVER is closed.
disagreed_ramp_s2026.pt     # 0.8574 peak e7, CONVERGED. Same argument as certainty_ramp above and the same
                            # family verdict; seated on merit so the pool is complete, not because the ramp
                            # earned anything. Re-open the LEVER only where supervision is thin, which is the
                            # condition ramp_dense_gate's decline named and no ramp arm has ever been run under.
                            # From the row this one replaced: against its matched control disagreed_uniform
                            # (0.8507) the RAMPED weighting reads +0.0067, which is the only reading on that
                            # pair. It does not survive the three-arm family read against calib_dense_hold.
unread_dense_s2026.pt       # 0.8577 peak e11 of 12, CONVERGED. Level with band_dense 0.8578 (-0.0001, well
                            # inside the 0.0062 floor) while trained on a DIFFERENT supervision signal:
                            # 27.3% of its targets come from unread-report derivation rather than the gold
                            # labels. The LABEL LANE it was armed to open is closed — the arm read null at
                            # +0.0020 on gold-58 and both named fallbacks reach fewer cells, so their ceiling
                            # is lower. What seats here is the CHECKPOINT, on merit and on the only kind of
                            # diversity the pool does not already have; the LEVER is closed and stays closed.

# Added 2026-09-05, the five `roster_check` found scoreable and in neither file. All five are SEATED
# rather than declined, on the owner's standing rule that a member below the best solo can still pay in
# an ensemble: what a seat buys is where a member is WRONG, not how often. The label lever they came from
# is closed (see the ledger sections `errors_rank`, `errors_relabel`, `neighbour_errors`) — the lever is
# what is closed, never the checkpoint, and these are checkpoints.
errors_relabel_s2026.pt     # 0.8522 solo, and the only member trained on a CORRECTED label table (1,932
                            # cells relabelled at the net-benefit-optimal budget). Its supervision differs
                            # from every other member's on exactly the cells the reader most likely got
                            # wrong, which is a diversity axis nothing else in the pool carries.
errors_rank_s2026.pt        # 0.8462 solo, trained with the same detector's ranking used to PRUNE rather
                            # than to correct. Same axis as above and the opposite treatment, so the two
                            # disagree with each other as well as with the pool.
blendema224_s2026.pt        # 0.8567 solo at the cheap 224 corner, blendhold plus --ema. Scores 0.0008
                            # BELOW its own control, which is inside the paired floor and therefore not
                            # a ranking; seated for the different weight trajectory an EMA leaves, not
                            # for the score. Its reading is logs/blendema224_ledger.log.
blendemalabel224_s2026.pt   # 0.8591 solo, the best 224-corner member the project owns. Three terms on the
                            # bare native224 base - blended labels, --ema, --slice-pooling labelwise - read
                            # +0.0089 over it, 1.4 paired floors, which is the readable comparison
                            # blendema224 could not make. Against the best single term (blendhold 0.8575) it
                            # is +0.0016, inside the floor and NOT a ranking. Its reading is
                            # logs/blendemalabel224_ledger.log.
chaindense_s2026.pt         # 0.8628 solo at the dense corner - the three 224-corner terms (blended labels,
                            # --ema, --slice-pooling labelwise) on the BARE dense base band_dense_hold
                            # (0.8573), +0.0055, 0.89 paired floors, INSIDE the floor and its arm's MIDDLE
                            # branch. Seated for DIVERSITY, not for rank: at 0.0014 BELOW the pool best it
                            # is not a ranking member, but it is the only member trained on blend_three_v1
                            # at 336 px with an EMA trajectory, so its errors are not the calibrated
                            # members' errors. The sentence that matters is in its ledger: it reads 0.0006
                            # under calib_dense_hold (0.8634), the same base plus --calibrated-targets
                            # ALONE, so three cheap terms and one expensive one are indistinguishable here
                            # and the chain SUBSTITUTES for calibration. Its reading is
                            # logs/chaindense_ledger.log.

chainfour_s2026.pt          # 0.8648 solo, the BEST single member this project owns, +0.0014 over
                            # calib_dense_hold (0.8634). Four terms on the dense base band_dense_hold
                            # (0.8573): --calibrated-targets, --labels blend_three_v1, --ema,
                            # --slice-pooling labelwise. Peak at e7 of a full 12, four declining epochs
                            # after it, so the number is a value and not a floor. Its arm's MIDDLE branch:
                            # the four terms sum to +0.0191 alone and delivered +0.0075 together, 39% -
                            # they substitute rather than add at the top. Seated for RANK, and its rank
                            # is the only thing it brings: on the five-seat held-twin proxy it adds
                            # +0.0020 alone but +0.0000 on top of chaindense/blendemalabel224/blendema224,
                            # which is why kneemri-proxyseat ships nine seats and not ten. Best solo,
                            # redundant in ensemble - the third time this project has measured that.
                            # Its reading is logs/chainfour_ledger.log.


clean_calib_s2026.pt        # 0.8649 ledger (peak e9 of 12) / 0.8936 on the 896 L75mid — NINTH-BEST SOLO of
                            # 262 honest members (#3 on HIS>=.75, #6 on R1 mid, #8 on R6 cut.75), ACL 0.944
                            # is 4th in the whole pool. Seated NEVER: swap for calib_span -0.0008, corr
                            # guard fails (block 0.871 -> 0.889), sixth seat +0.0001. On the roster for the
                            # SOLO, which is what a roster records; the seat argument is in the ledger row
                            # (2026-09-07) and in D46. It redistributes columns rather than lifting them.

labelwise_extended_s2026.pt # 0.8623 ledger (peak e8) / 0.8986 L75 over 909 rows - the BEST of the ten
                            # members roster_check found undocumented on 2026-09-08, and above most of
                            # what is already packaged. A labelwise head on the extended crop; on the
                            # roster for the solo, no seat argument attached (none has been measured).
extended_band_s2026.pt      # 0.8519 ledger (peak e9) / 0.8847 L75 over 909 rows. The extended crop under
                            # the 0.1-0.9 band, converged, and the second of the ten undocumented members
                            # worth shipping. Its two re-runs are declined (both died early).
latent_register_dense_s2026.pt  # 0.8385 ledger (peak e10 of 12, n=909, midpoint), converged flat over the
                            # last three epochs. Rostered for DIVERSITY, not for its solo: it is the only
                            # v3small trunk in the pool carrying an on-domain latent-MIM adaptation, and
                            # the pool is dinov2-heavy. Its solo prices against nothing until
                            # v3small_control lands (knee-j2ovn) -- the only same-recipe v3small run on
                            # disk, errors_v3small at 0.8280, differs in two ways at once. Seat value is
                            # seat_value's call, and it is not blocked on that control.
fovjitter160_s2026.pt       # 0.8545 kept — above the 0.8521 seat bar, and the pool's only member trained
                            # with a VARYING field extent (160 mm nominal, jittered per study). Its own
                            # question read NULL (decode -0.0297 against crop160_span's -0.0265, inside
                            # the pre-registered null band, ledger 2026-09-09): jitter is not the transfer
                            # mechanism. That closes the ARM, not the MEMBER — a null on the decode axis
                            # is not an argument against a 0.8545 solo, and every other member on this
                            # roster saw one fixed extent. Rostered on solo plus that one structural
                            # difference; whether it earns a seat is seat_value's call, not this file's.
